DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  cclloossee__rraannggee()  system  call  closes all open file descriptors from
       _f_i_r_s_t to _l_a_s_t (included).

       Errors closing a given file descriptor are currently ignored.

       _f_l_a_g_s is a bit mask containing 0 or more of the following:

       CCLLOOSSEE__RRAANNGGEE__CCLLOOEEXXEECC (since Linux 5.11)
              Set the close‐on‐exec flag on the  specified  file  descriptors,
              rather than immediately closing them.

       CCLLOOSSEE__RRAANNGGEE__UUNNSSHHAARREE
              Unshare  the specified file descriptors from any other processes
              before closing them, avoiding races with other  threads  sharing
              the file descriptor table.

